  "question": {
    "text": "A bus is moving with a velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi></math>towards a huge wall. The driver sounds a horn of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>165</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. If the speed of sound in air is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>335</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the number of beats heard per second by a passenger inside the bus will be"
